<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uzgen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Özgön</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uzgen is a town in the Osh Region of Kyrgyzstan, in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergana-valley">Fergana Valley</a>. In the eleventh and twelfth centuries it was a capital and royal burial place of the Kara-Khanid dynasty, and a brick minaret and three richly decorated mausoleums from that period survive. Located on routes between Fergana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a>, it remains a market town known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uzgen.jpg" alt="Uzgen" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikolaus · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uzgen_Mausoleum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
